cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Gigi in research, please cite the software release you used. Where a specific algorithm specification, verifier or divergence finding informed
  your work, the contributors for it are recorded in that algorithm's algorithm.yaml and in people/people.yaml.
title: "Gigi: an executable registry of graph algorithm semantics"
abstract: >-
  Gigi records what graph algorithms mean, runs them across multiple engines, and verifies the differences it finds. Registry claims are executable: every
  declared cross-engine divergence is reproduced in continuous integration, and an undeclared difference fails the build.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/graphgeeks-lab/gigi-algo
authors:
  - given-names: Dennis
    family-names: Irorere
    affiliation: GraphGeeks
keywords:
  - graph algorithms
  - verification
  - reproducibility
  - provenance
  - network analysis
